{"q":"713","t":"Subarray Product Less Than K","d":"Medium","p":false,"c":"<p>Given an array of integers <code>nums</code> and an integer <code>k</code>, return <em>the number of contiguous subarrays where the product of all the elements in the subarray is strictly less than </em><code>k</code>.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p>\n\n<pre>\n<strong>Input:</strong> nums = [10,5,2,6], k = 100\n<strong>Output:</strong> 8\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> The 8 subarrays that have product less than 100 are:\n[10], [5], [2], [6], [10, 5], [5, 2], [2, 6], [5, 2, 6]\nNote that [10, 5, 2] is not included as the product of 100 is not strictly less than k.\n</pre>\n\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p>\n\n<pre>\n<strong>Input:</strong> nums = [1,2,3], k = 0\n<strong>Output:</strong> 0\n</pre>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= nums.length &lt;= 3 * 10<sup>4</sup></code></li>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= nums[i] &lt;= 1000</code></li>\n\t<li><code>0 &lt;= k &lt;= 10<sup>6</sup></code></li>\n</ul>\n","h":["For each j, let opt(j) be the smallest i so that nums[i] * nums[i+1] * ... * nums[j] is less than k.  opt is an increasing function."],"m":"{\r\n  \"name\": \"numSubarrayProductLessThanK\",\r\n  \"params\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"name\": \"nums\",\r\n      \"type\": \"integer[]\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"name\": \"k\",\r\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"return\": {\r\n    \"type\": \"integer\"\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n","g":[{"name":"Array","slug":"array"},{"name":"Binary Search","slug":"binary-search"},{"name":"Sliding Window","slug":"sliding-window"},{"name":"Prefix Sum","slug":"prefix-sum"}],"s":[{"t":"Maximum Product Subarray","s":"maximum-product-subarray","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Maximum Size Subarray Sum Equals k","s":"maximum-size-subarray-sum-equals-k","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Subarray Sum Equals K","s":"subarray-sum-equals-k","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Two Sum Less Than K","s":"two-sum-less-than-k","d":"Easy","p":false},{"t":"Number of Smooth Descent Periods of a Stock","s":"number-of-smooth-descent-periods-of-a-stock","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Count Subarrays With Score Less Than K","s":"count-subarrays-with-score-less-than-k","d":"Hard","p":false}],"co":[["Apple","apple"],["Meta","facebook"],["Google","google"],["Amazon","amazon"],["Meesho","meesho"],["Bloomberg","bloomberg"],["Salesforce","salesforce"],["Squarepoint Capital","squarepoint-capital"],["Airbnb","airbnb"],["Samsung","samsung"],["Microsoft","microsoft"],["Agoda","agoda"],["Yatra","yatra"]],"cs":{"a":[["Google","google",6],["Meta","facebook",2],["Amazon","amazon",2],["Apple","apple",2],["Meesho","meesho",2]],"b":[],"m":[["Salesforce","salesforce",14],["Bloomberg","bloomberg",9],["Microsoft","microsoft",5],["Airbnb","airbnb",5],["Squarepoint Capital","squarepoint-capital",5],["Samsung","samsung",4],["Oracle","oracle",3],["tcs","tcs",2],["Tekion","tekion",2],["Agoda","agoda",2]]}}